<body>
<div class="poster">

  <!-- HEADER -->
  <div class="header">
    <div class="header-label">Global Education Data</div>
    <h1>The State of Global Education</h1>
    <div class="header-subtitle">A comparative look at how far the world has come in expanding education access — and the critical gaps that remain in quality, attendance, and equity.</div>
    <div class="header-accent-line"></div>
  </div>

  <!-- SECTION 1: HISTORICAL PROGRESS -->
  <div class="section">
    <div class="progress-section">
      <div class="section-label">Historical Transformation</div>
      <div class="section-title">Two Centuries of Educational Expansion</div>
      <div class="progress-row">
        <div class="progress-block">
          <div class="progress-year">1 8 0 0</div>
          <div class="progress-number negative">&lt; 1 in 5</div>
          <div class="progress-desc">Adults with any formal education</div>
        </div>
        <div class="progress-arrow">&rarr;</div>
        <div class="progress-block">
          <div class="progress-year">T O D A Y</div>
          <div class="progress-number positive">&gt; 4 in 5</div>
          <div class="progress-desc">Adults with any formal education</div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="icon-arrays">
        <div class="icon-array-group">
          <div class="icon-row">
            <div class="icon-dot lit"></div>
            <div class="icon-dot dim"></div>
            <div class="icon-dot dim"></div>
            <div class="icon-dot dim"></div>
            <div class="icon-dot dim"></div>
            <div class="icon-dot dim"></div>
            <div class="icon-dot dim"></div>
            <div class="icon-dot dim"></div>
            <div class="icon-dot dim"></div>
            <div class="icon-dot dim"></div>
          </div>
          <div class="icon-array-caption">1800: Fewer than 1 in 5 adults educated</div>
        </div>
        <div class="icon-array-group">
          <div class="icon-row">
            <div class="icon-dot teal"></div>
            <div class="icon-dot teal"></div>
            <div class="icon-dot teal"></div>
            <div class="icon-dot teal"></div>
            <div class="icon-dot teal"></div>
            <div class="icon-dot teal"></div>
            <div class="icon-dot teal"></div>
            <div class="icon-dot teal"></div>
            <div class="icon-dot dim"></div>
            <div class="icon-dot dim"></div>
          </div>
          <div class="icon-array-caption">Today: More than 4 in 5 adults educated</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- SECTION 2: 244 MILLION — DOMINANT -->
  <div class="section">
    <div class="out-of-school-section">
      <div class="section-label" style="position:relative;">The Crisis Today</div>
      <div class="big-stat-number">244</div>
      <div class="big-stat-unit">Million Children</div>
      <div class="big-stat-desc">Still out of school worldwide (2023)</div>
      <div class="breakdown-row">
        <div class="breakdown-item">
          <div class="breakdown-number">~60M</div>
          <div class="breakdown-label">Primary-age children out of school</div>
        </div>
        <div class="breakdown-item">
          <div class="breakdown-number">~184M</div>
          <div class="breakdown-label">Secondary-age adolescents out of school</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- SECTION 3: LEARNING CRISIS -->
  <div class="section">
    <div class="learning-section">
      <div class="learning-left">
        <div class="section-label">Hidden Crisis</div>
        <div class="learning-equation">
          <span class="enroll">Enrollment</span>
          <span class="neq"> &ne; </span>
          <span class="learn">Learning</span>
        </div>
        <div class="learning-stat">&lt; 20%</div>
        <div class="learning-stat-desc">of children in low-income countries achieve minimum reading proficiency by the end of primary school — they cannot identify key ideas or connect them to their experiences.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="learning-right">
        <div id="chart-learning" class="chart-container"></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- SECTION 4: QUALITY INEQUALITY -->
  <div class="section">
    <div class="quality-section">
      <div class="section-label">Quality Gap</div>
      <div class="section-title">Learning-Adjusted Years of Schooling: A World Divided</div>
      <div class="quality-comparison">
        <div class="quality-side poor">
          <div class="quality-side-label">Poorest Countries</div>
          <div class="quality-number">&lt; 3</div>
          <div class="quality-unit">years of quality schooling</div>
          <div class="quality-desc">Parts of Sub-Saharan Africa</div>
          <div class="quality-bar-wrap">
            <div class="quality-bar-bg"><div class="quality-bar-fill"></div></div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="quality-vs">
          <div class="quality-vs-text">VS</div>
        </div>
        <div class="quality-side rich">
          <div class="quality-side-label">Richest Countries</div>
          <div class="quality-number">10+</div>
          <div class="quality-unit">years of quality schooling</div>
          <div class="quality-desc">High-income nations</div>
          <div class="quality-bar-wrap">
            <div class="quality-bar-bg"><div class="quality-bar-fill"></div></div>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="quality-middle">
        <div class="quality-middle-stat">
          <div class="quality-middle-number">&lt; 7 years</div>
          <div class="quality-middle-label">South Asia &amp; Sub-Saharan Africa average — where most of the world's children live</div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- SECTION 5: GENDER GAP -->
  <div class="section">
    <div class="gender-section">
      <div class="section-label">Progress</div>
      <div class="section-title">Closing the Gender Gap</div>
      <div class="gender-grid">
        <div class="gender-card">
          <div class="gender-level">Primary Education</div>
          <div class="gender-status closed"><span class="status-icon check">&#10003;</span>Nearly Closed</div>
          <div class="gender-detail">Gender gap in enrollment has largely closed globally</div>
        </div>
        <div class="gender-card">
          <div class="gender-level">Secondary Education</div>
          <div class="gender-status closed"><span class="status-icon check">&#10003;</span>Nearly Closed</div>
          <div class="gender-detail">Parity achieved in most regions worldwide</div>
        </div>
        <div class="gender-card">
          <div class="gender-level">Tertiary Education</div>
          <div class="gender-status exceed"><span class="status-icon up">&#8593;</span>Women Exceed Men</div>
          <div class="gender-detail">Young women now more likely to be enrolled than young men</div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="gender-exception">
        <strong>Notable exception:</strong> In countries like Afghanistan, girls remain far less likely to attend school at any level.
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- SECTION 6: KEY TAKEAWAY -->
  <div class="section">
    <div class="takeaway-section">
      <div class="takeaway-label">Key Takeaway</div>
      <div class="takeaway-text">
        The world has achieved <strong>remarkable progress</strong> — but the job is far from done.
        <strong>Hundreds of millions</strong> of children are either out of school or learning very little while in it.
        Closing the gap between enrollment and actual learning, and between rich and poor nations,
        is one of the <strong>most pressing challenges</strong> of our time.
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <!-- FOOTER -->
  <div class="footer">
    <div class="footer-text">Sources: UNESCO Institute for Statistics &middot; World Bank &middot; Global Education Monitoring Report &middot; Our World in Data</div>
  </div>

</div>

<!-- AntV Infographic Charts -->
<script src="/app/vendor/infographic.min.js"></script>
<script>
  // Donut chart for reading proficiency
  const chartLearning = new AntVInfographic.Infographic({
    container: '#chart-learning',
    width: 440,
    height: 300,
  });

  const learningSyntax = `infographic chart-pie-donut-plain-text
data
  title Reading Proficiency
  desc Low-income countries
  values
    - label Proficient
      value 17
    - label Not Proficient
      value 83
theme
  palette #14B8A6 #FF6347`;

  chartLearning.render(learningSyntax);
  document.fonts?.ready.then(() => {
    chartLearning.render(learningSyntax);
  }).catch((e) => console.error('Font load error:', e));
</script>
</body>
