    <div class="s-gender">
      <div class="section-tag">Progress</div>
      <div class="section-heading">Closing the Gender Gap</div>
      <div class="gender-row">
        <div class="gender-card">
          <div class="g-level">Primary Education</div>
          <div class="g-status ok"><span class="g-icon g">&#10003;</span>Nearly Closed</div>
          <div class="g-detail">Gender gap largely closed globally</div>
        </div>
        <div class="gender-card">
          <div class="g-level">Secondary Education</div>
          <div class="g-status ok"><span class="g-icon g">&#10003;</span>Nearly Closed</div>
          <div class="g-detail">Parity achieved in most regions</div>
        </div>
        <div class="gender-card">
          <div class="g-level">Tertiary Education</div>
          <div class="g-status up"><span class="g-icon a">&#8593;</span>Women Exceed Men</div>
          <div class="g-detail">Women now more likely to be enrolled</div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="g-exception">
        <strong>Notable exception:</strong> In countries like Afghanistan, girls remain far less likely to attend school at any level.
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <!-- S6: KEY TAKEAWAY -->
  <section class="section">
    <div class="s-takeaway">
      <div class="take-tag">Key Takeaway</div>
      <p class="take-text">
        The world has achieved <strong>remarkable progress</strong> — but the job is far from done.
        <strong>Hundreds of millions</strong> of children are either out of school or learning very little while in it.
        Closing the gap between enrollment and actual learning, and between rich and poor nations,
        is one of the <strong>most pressing challenges</strong> of our time.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

